WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.012 --> 00:00:05.934
"Ah-choo!" Arthur sneezed loudly into his hands.

2
00:00:06.074 --> 00:00:09.817
"Arthur, don't you have a tissue?

3
00:00:09.897 --> 00:00:13.639
Please sneeze into your arm, not your hands," Mrs.

4
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:15.880
MacPhee said.

5
00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:33.737
"Why?" Arthur asked.

6
00:00:34.678 --> 00:00:37.299
He held up his hands and wiggled his fingers.

7
00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:42.182
"I can catch the sneeze droplets better with my hands."

8
00:00:42.202 --> 00:00:50.606
"Cold germs spread very easily―especially after a sneeze," the teacher said.

9
00:00:50.626 --> 00:00:57.370
"Every time you touch something, you could spread your cold germs."

10
00:01:01.164 --> 00:01:04.085
"Eww!" Sarah said, leaning away from Arthur.

11
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:10.287
"Rhinoviruses are the most common cold viruses," Mrs.

12
00:01:10.347 --> 00:01:11.127
MacPhee said.

13
00:01:11.147 --> 00:01:17.248
"They can live for up to 24 hours outside of the body.

14
00:01:19.969 --> 00:01:24.530
They can even live on things like computer keyboards and doorknobs."

15
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:32.209
"So if I use the computer after Arthur, I might get a cold too?"

16
00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:33.709
Sarah asked.

17
00:01:38.451 --> 00:01:39.431
The teacher nodded.

18
00:01:39.451 --> 00:01:43.572
"Even hours after Arthur used it."

19
00:01:48.454 --> 00:01:49.854
sounds like 'rhinoceros!'"

20
00:01:50.194 --> 00:01:50.915
Cody said.

21
00:01:52.695 --> 00:01:53.896
The teacher laughed.

22
00:01:56.244 --> 00:02:00.147
"The word 'rhinovirus' comes from the Greek word for 'nose.'"

23
00:02:06.271 --> 00:02:11.094
"I've had four colds already this winter," Sarah complained.

24
00:02:11.114 --> 00:02:17.599
"Most children get eight to twelve colds a year," the teacher explained.

25
00:02:17.619 --> 00:02:24.564
"There are over two hundred different viruses that cause the common cold.

26
00:02:26.748 --> 00:02:30.009
Adults get only two to four colds each year.

27
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:35.791
That's because they've already been exposed to many of the viruses."

28
00:02:39.432 --> 00:02:40.772
Cody put up his hand.

29
00:02:40.792 --> 00:02:46.274
"I read that sneeze droplets can travel almost two meters."

30
00:02:49.615 --> 00:02:50.675
Sarah frowned.

31
00:02:50.695 --> 00:02:52.816
"That's disgusting."

32
00:02:55.032 --> 00:02:58.034
"How do you think we can avoid catching a cold?"

33
00:02:58.374 --> 00:02:59.615
Mrs. MacPhee asked.

34
00:03:03.697 --> 00:03:06.919
two meters away from somebody who is about to sneeze?"

35
00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:08.139
Cody guessed.

36
00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.162
"That's not always possible," the teacher said.

37
00:03:17.045 --> 00:03:17.805
other ideas?"

38
00:03:20.086 --> 00:03:22.888
Sarah pointed to the sink at the back of the classroom.

39
00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:25.629
"Wash our hands with soap?"

40
00:03:27.789 --> 00:03:30.050
"Excellent idea, Sarah," Mrs.

41
00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:30.870
MacPhee said.

42
00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:38.532
"We should wash our hands in warm, soapy water for at least twenty seconds.

43
00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:41.073
This gets rid of the germs."

44
00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:45.995
Arthur put both hands over his nose and tilted his head back.

45
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.382
"Ahh ahh The other students all leaned away from Arthur.

46
00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:58.245
Arthur put down his hands and grinned.

47
00:03:58.265 --> 00:04:00.966
"Just kidding.

48
00:04:01.427 --> 00:04:03.928
I wanted to see if you were paying attention."

49
00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:09.352
"It's almost lunchtime.

50
00:04:10.393 --> 00:04:13.455
Everyone, please line up to wash your hands."

51
00:04:13.935 --> 00:04:15.856
Mrs. MacPhee smiled at Arthur.

52
00:04:15.876 --> 00:04:20.840
"Arthur, maybe you should go first!"
